<metadata_system id="159" name="iOS Photo Library Metadata" category="IMG" category_label="Images" used_for="iPhone/iPad photo library — Apple PhotoKit (PHAsset)" spec_source="Apple PhotoKit framework (developer.apple.com/documentation/photos) + Photos.sqlite schema" completeness="comprehensive" record_count="48">
  <description>Apple's PhotoKit (Photos framework) provides the API for the iOS/macOS photo library. The central object is PHAsset — a representation of an image, video, or Live Photo. Each asset has rich metadata beyond what's stored in the file itself: burst grouping, edit/adjustment tracking, source classification (camera, screenshot, downloaded), iCloud sync state, scene classification (CV-derived), face recognition links, and album/collection memberships. The underlying Photos.sqlite database (forensically significant) tracks all of this. This entry covers PHAsset properties, mediaSubtype flags (Live Photo, Portrait, Slo-mo, Cinematic, Spatial), PHAssetResource types, PHImageManager request parameters, PHAssetCollection types, and the on-disk storage layout including originals, derivatives, mutations (edit history), and the SQLite schema.</description>
